  "reason": "For #228, after a second review of the follow-up of #225: DEC-116 says a build script's output is told by cargo's form of the package directory, and that rust-test reads the crates of a project by the one rule of rust-item; DEC-90 and DEC-99 say the same of the manifests read; V-145 and V-111 say what the new tests hold (a link at the top of the docs passed over, a look-alike path compared, the reason that names a crate and the one whose pages are missing, a crate at the top of a project with no manifest at its root read by rust-test). Read against the code by its author; what each document claims still holds, by the tests it names, which are left to CI on the pull request",
